  "releaseNotes": "## 12.1.2\n\n### Fixes\n- Inline formatting — including superscript and subscript — is now reliably carried to the new paragraph on Enter and across block splits, including splits that occur past a trailing line break.\n- A pending springloaded format is now honored when formatting is carried across a block split, so toggling a format off just before a split is respected in the new block.\n- When a delete empties a block, the caret now stays in that block instead of moving elsewhere.\n- After a deletion the caret keeps backward gravity, so formatting queried at the caret reflects the text that remains.\n- The selection now collapses after paste and delete operations.\n- The formatting-property registry is now thread-safe.\n- Materialized elements are now held strongly from their document node, preventing them from being collected while still referenced by the live tree.",
